# Byte-exact round-trip is a HARD REQUIREMENT for this repository.
#
# Every file under repro_package_zp/ has its sha256 recorded in
# repro_package_zp/manifests/CHECKSUMS.txt and MANIFEST.json, and
# manifests/SEAL.txt pins the sha256 of MANIFEST.json itself.  Any
# line-ending normalisation (git's core.autocrlf on Windows) would change
# the bytes on checkout, so a verifier on Windows and a verifier on Linux
# would compute different hashes for the same commit and the seal would
# appear broken.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion, so a checkout is
# byte-identical to the commit on every platform.  Diffs still work; only
# conversion is off.
* -text
